1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,440
Did you know that you can feel very lonely when you're around people.
你知道吗？即使周围有人，你也可能感到很孤独。

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:06,400
This is actually pretty common but no one teaches you about it.
这其实很常见，但没有人教你认识这件事。

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:12,479
Because all you hear is that loneliness is the absence of people when really it is the absence of understanding.
因为你听到的都是，孤独就是身边没有人；可她认为，真正缺少的是理解。

4
00:00:12,479 --> 00:00:20,390
It is feeling alone it is realizing that nobody gets you.
是感到孤单，是意识到没有人懂你。

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,959
Loneliness has always been painted as a bad thing.
孤独一直被描绘成一件坏事。

6
00:00:22,959 --> 00:00:28,720
And it is actually because studies show that loneliness increases your chances of getting many lifestyle diseases.
她说孤独确实不好，因为有研究显示，它会增加患多种生活方式相关疾病的概率。

7
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:32,549
But what I find funny is that our society says that loneliness is bad.
但她觉得讽刺的是，我们的社会说孤独不好。

8
00:00:32,559 --> 00:00:43,120
And yet the systems that run this same society such as the patriarchy capitalism all forms of discrimination they only thrive because of the loneliness of the majority.
然而，她认为，维持这个社会的父权制、资本主义和各种歧视，却依赖多数人的孤独才得以兴盛。

9
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:50,879
So it's really a big paradox that the same society that wants you to be lonely for it to exist also shames you for your feelings of loneliness.
因此她说，这很矛盾：同一个社会需要你的孤独才能存在，却又羞辱你的孤独感。

10
00:00:50,879 --> 00:00:55,039
The meaning of loneliness has always been about the absence of people around you.
孤独的含义一直被说成是周围没有人。

11
00:00:55,039 --> 00:00:59,510
This is why many young people are pushed to be in relationships so they aren't lonely.
她认为，这就是许多年轻人被催促进入恋爱关系的原因，好让他们不孤独。

12
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:03,760
This is why people stay in friendships that are bad for them just so that they are not lonely.
这也是人们留在对自己有害的友谊中的原因，仅仅为了不孤独。

13
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:07,440
Being alone has always been used as a substitute for loneliness.
独处总是被当作孤独的替代说法。

14
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:11,040
And this isn't actually true because there are many people who are alone but not lonely.
但她认为这并不准确，因为有人独处却不孤独。

15
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:14,080
And then there are those who are actually alone and also lonely.
也有人确实既独自一人，又感到孤独。

16
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:18,550
The invisible part of this equation is whether or not the individual has chosen to be alone.
这里隐而未见的因素，是这个人是否主动选择了独处。

17
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:22,959
Actually this touches on just one type of loneliness social loneliness.
其实，这只涉及一种孤独：社交孤独。

18
00:01:22,959 --> 00:01:28,639
And I would say extroverts would suffer from this a lot because they need to be around people to recharge their batteries.
她觉得外向者尤其容易受这种孤独影响，因为他们需要和人在一起来恢复精力。

19
00:01:28,639 --> 00:01:32,880
However there are more types that are rarely spoken about such as emotional loneliness.
然而，还有些类型很少被谈起，比如情感上的孤独。

20
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:39,360
I'd say majority of people in the world of today suffer from this it is to be expected in a society that demonizes emotions.
她说，当今世界大多数人都受这种孤独困扰；在一个把情绪妖魔化的社会里，这是可以预料的。

21
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:43,680
You can be around people you love and still feel like you don't belong like you are an impostor.
你可能和爱的人在一起，仍觉得自己不属于这里，像一个冒充者。

22
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:47,279
How many african families create space for their children to just be.
她问，有多少非洲家庭能给孩子空间，让他们自在地做自己？

23
00:01:47,279 --> 00:01:51,110
And actually many children face loneliness right from their own homes.
而且，许多孩子正是在自己家中就感到孤独。

24
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:56,880
And you know what you don't even need to be told anything directly to know that those around you don't want someone like you.
你知道吗，你甚至不需要听到别人直接对你说什么，就能知道身边的人不想接纳像你这样的人。

25
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,760
You just have to listen to how they talk about other people.
你只需要听听他们如何谈论别人。

26
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:09,439
I always find it so interesting when something happens to someone and their family members say but why didn't they just come to us for help why didn't they just speak to us.
她总觉得很耐人寻味：有人出了事，家人却说，为什么不来找我们帮忙？为什么不跟我们说？

27
00:02:09,439 --> 00:02:17,200
Why would anyone come to you for help when they have heard you a million times saying negative things about those who are in the same situation you find yourself in.
可如果他们无数次听见你贬低那些处境与自己相同的人，为什么还会来向你求助？

28
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:19,990
In a society that is always blaming victims.
在一个总是责怪受害者的社会里——

29
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,920
Why is it hard to believe that people would rather give up on living rather than speak about the atrocities they have gone through.
为什么难以相信，有人宁愿放弃生活，也不愿讲出自己经历过的暴行？

30
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:29,360
Why would they speak when they see how you treat those who have spoken.
他们看到你怎样对待已经发声的人，为什么还要开口？

31
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:33,840
Why would they trust you when they have seen how you've treated those who trusted you.
他们看过你如何对待曾信任你的人，为什么还会信任你？

32
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,760
The things you said behind their backs.
还有你在他们背后说过的话——

33
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:41,200
The rumors you created about how they must have done things to deserve whatever came their way.
以及你编造的传言，说他们肯定做过什么，才落得这样的遭遇。

34
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:45,040
When people tell me that I'm a failure because I came back home in my late 20 ies.
当人们说我是失败者，因为我在二十多岁后期回了家——〔字幕 20 ies 疑似年龄识别，待听辨〕

35
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:50,390
I'm always intrigued by their thought process and it always ends at why would you even just go back home.
她总对他们的思路感到好奇，而最后总会落到一句：你为什么要回家？

36
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:54,880
Their discomfort comes from being home because a lot of them didn't like their own homes.
他们的不适来自回家这件事，因为其中很多人本来就不喜欢自己的家。

37
00:02:54,880 --> 00:03:02,709
And actually I also never liked being home and this is the first time in my life that I've spent an entire full year at home without break.
而她自己以前也不喜欢待在家里；这是她人生中第一次连续一整年待在家，没有中断。
